# MODEL: 256
# Rx_Coro.in (a point source, nGridpts= 511) at model 256 (macos 2026-10-10).  The
# load clamps the grid to the model (the long-standing "Too many grid points" reset,
# CLI macosio.F and SMACOS smacosio.F alike), and the trace must complete.  The defect
# behind it: PtSource placed an EVEN grid one row high, so the clamped 256-point grid
# wrote RayID(., 257) -- the gfortran DEBUG build aborted there (measured 2026-10-10);
# the release build overran by one row silently, so on release this journal is a
# no-crash regression gate, not a must-fail.
old $RES/pymacos/tests/Rx/Rx_Coro.in
opd 21
/null
# EXPECT: Too many grid points\. Resetting npts to\s+256
# EXPECT: RMS OPD error is
